The biggest problems are:

Frontend: main.js is loaded on your login page even though it is meant for the animal page.
Frontend: email is not defined/persisted after login.
Frontend: getElementById("DOMContentLoaded", "videos") is incorrect.
Frontend/backend: your frontend creates an account with only email and password, but the backend requires firstName and lastName.
Frontend/backend: the backend hashes passwords with bcrypt, but the login frontend compares the password as plain text.
Backend: /updateDone uses accounts.updateOne(...), but accounts doesn't exist there. You created collection.
Backend: /updateDone contains duplicated/unreachable code after res.json().
Backend: you're exposing all accounts and their password hashes through /allAccounts. That's a serious security problem.
